# SRG-APP-000164-AU-002480  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must be configured to enforce a minimum
# 15-character password length.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000164-AU-002480
group:           V-206467
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-004066
control_rev5:    IA-5

contribution:    Splunk's native authentication enforces a minimum password length for
                 every password set or changed on an account it holds, and the product STIG
                 names the value.

governs:         authentication.conf - How users sign in, and the password rules applied to local accounts.

check:           authentication.conf [splunk_auth] minPasswordLength min 15
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          authentication.conf [splunk_auth] minPasswordLength https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-cloud-platform/administer/manage-users-and-security/10.2.2510/manage-credentials-and-keys/configure-a-splunk-enterprise-password-policy-using-the-authentication.conf-configuration-file
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Where authType is LDAP or SAML, the directory service or identity provider
                 enforces length for federated accounts; [splunk_auth] then still governs
                 the native accounts that remain, including the emergency account of last
                 resort
external:        Operating system account passwords on the host

citation:        SPLK-CL-000370 check text ("If the minPasswordLength is missing or is
                 configured to 14 or less, this is a finding") and fix text
                 ("minPasswordLength = 15 or more"); authentication.conf.spec:437-449
                 (minPasswordLength, positive integer, default 8, rejects non-conforming
                 password changes)
finding:         authentication.conf [splunk_auth] minPasswordLength is absent or below 15,
                 so the application accepts native account passwords shorter than the
                 required minimum.
